# team/formats — sealed memfd data segment, fd passed once, mapping cached
#
# Change: the worker backs each data segment with an anonymous memfd
# (memfd_create + one ftruncate + MADV_HUGEPAGE + F_SEAL_SHRINK|F_SEAL_GROW),
# hands the descriptor to the client once over an AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET
# connection (SCM_RIGHTS), and both sides keep their mapping for the life of
# the worker/process. FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 opts in; the default remains the
# named /dev/shm segment. Frames and ring ops are unchanged.
#
# The same command is run on both images, one at a time, under
# /tmp/fpq-bench.lock. FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 is present on both runs; the
# baseline client/worker ignore it.

## Build (change image, from this worktree)

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker build -q --target dev -t fpq-formats -f docker/Dockerfile .'
    -> sha256:520ef97289323fc4493764a762aadf35ac7dedff3eff5b52e3fdfa551e0d6d28

## Command — 100K

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline -e FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 100000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=formats  -e FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 fpq-formats  benchmarks.sh 100000'

## Command — 3K (small-batch read)

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline -e FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 fpq-baseline benchmarks.sh 3000'
    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=formats  -e FASTPOSTGRES_MEMFD=1 fpq-formats  benchmarks.sh 3000'

Five alternating repetitions per image and size. The result lines quoted in
the A/B are medians; every per-run value is listed so the spread travels with
the number. (This benchmark's process-to-process spread is several percent,
and larger on the 3K size.)

